 "monotonicity_correction_note": "The original monotonicity case construction (append one unknown-type operation to an otherwise-clean route) did not exercise the actual historical bug: _check_operation_order EXCLUDES any adjacent pair touching an unrecognized op type from both `assessed` and `violations` (confirmed by direct source inspection after the first run showed 200/200 'violations' on current HEAD, which is impossible given finding 21's 0.994 mean and the 43-assertion test suite -- a self-contradiction that triggered this re-check rather than being reported as a validator regression). The bug/fix is specifically about assessed==0 (a route of ENTIRELY unrecognized op types): 1.0 pre-fix, 0.5 post-fix, per validator.py's own comment. Re-run with the corrected construction (replace a route's operations with two unrecognized-type steps, direct exact-value check) and merged in -- this replaces the original monotonicity row/prediction inputs.",
 "atmosphere_test_power_gap_note": "token_identity and notation_atmosphere_synonym show ZERO violations on EVERY version tested, including the ones expected to be buggy (v0-v2 for token_identity; v0-v2 for notation_atmosphere_synonym) -- investigated directly rather than reported as a clean pass: _check_chempot_atmosphere only USES _classify_atmosphere's result when the target's own chempot envelope requires oxidizing or reducing conditions; in the \"flexible\" regime (neither required) it returns 1.0 regardless of the declared atmosphere string. Confirmed directly: 60/60 token_identity test cases (all real sampled targets with a heating operation) landed in the flexible regime, so H2 vs H2O vs O2 atmosphere strings scored identically (1.0) on every version -- the substring-trap code path was never exercised by this particular sample of targets. This is a TEST-POWER gap (confirmed via direct inspection of the raw chempot_atmosphere values and gradeability tags), not evidence the historical bug/fix doesn't exist or that these two axioms hold -- flagged honestly rather than reported as a pass. Overall prediction 1 (>=4/6 flagged) does not depend on these two, since scale + notation_hydrate + abstention + monotonicity already clear the >=4 bar on their own.",
